==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets Alloy invent a successful per-task operation whose (relationship, kind) pair is outside the permission matrix — the canonical least-privilege violation.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_003_MemberPermissions, FR_005_AdminPermissions, FR_019_AuditReadAccess
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_003_MemberPermissions: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_005_AdminPermissions: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_019_AuditReadAccess: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: Clears the cross-team / in-team-no-rel denial. The injected fact then forces an outsider-success operation to exist, which any byte-equivalent / no-leakage assertion must reject.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation, FR_014_ByteEquivalent, FR_004_NoUnauthorisedMember
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_014_ByteEquivalent: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_004_NoUnauthorisedMember: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OwnerOnlyShareControl  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_OwnerOnlyShareControl.als
    rationale: Removing the owner-only constraint on PatchShares lets a non-owner succeed at modifying the share list — exactly the Q1=A violation.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_010_OwnerOnlyShares
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_010_OwnerOnlyShares: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditOnMutation  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditOnMutation.als
    rationale: Without this fact, successful mutations may have zero audit entries (or failed ops may emit entries). The injected violation forces a successful PATCH with no audit entry — the canonical 'state change without audit' bug.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_AuditPerMutation, FR_018_AuditAtomic, ValidationBeforeMutation
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditPerMutation: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditAtomic: FAIL (expected)
      - ValidationBeforeMutation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets the audit entry's actor or role be unhooked from the calling operation — exactly the FR-002 attribution-correctness failure mode (role spoofed from body, etc.).
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_002_RoleFromToken
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_RoleFromToken: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditEntryUnique  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditEntryUnique.als
    rationale: Removing 'each AuditEntry has exactly one emitting Operation' allows the same audit row to be claimed by two operations — a structural mutation/duplication of an append-only artefact.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_017_AuditImmutable, AuditCompleteness, FR_015_AuditPerMutation
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditPerMutation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ShareeSameTeam  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_ShareeSameTeam.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact allows a sharee whose team differs from the task's team. The injected fact forces such a cross-team share to exist, violating FR-012.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_SameTeamShare
      - FR_012_SameTeamShare: FAIL (expected)

